Article 225 of the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China (2023 Amendment) [Article 225, Chapter 3, Section 8 of the General Part]  
Whoever commits any of the following acts of illegal business operations in violation of state regulations, thereby disturbing the order of the market and the circumstances are serious, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than five years or criminal detention, and shall also be fined an amount not less than but not more than five times the amount of illegal gains, or be fined alone:  
(1) operating items that are subject to state monopoly or restricted sale as stipulated by laws and administrative regulations without authorization;  
(2) trading import and export licenses, certificates of origin for import and export, or other operation permits or approval documents as stipulated by laws and administrative regulations;  
(3) operating securities, futures, or insurance businesses without approval from the competent state authorities, or illegally conducting payment settlement businesses;  
(4) other serious acts of illegal business operations disturbing the market order.

